  learned: "The brief said authentication. Testing said something else. People did not want the frame to prove itself; they wanted it to let them in. We rebuilt the idea around access rather than verification, and that finding has shaped every deployment since. The second lesson was cost: at atelier quality, two thousand one of ones did not clear the cost of making them."
